    },
    "body": "The supported geometric reader often finds useful source content but fails to finish a valid answer. This adds an opt-in exact-quarter warm start for the existing Period/Stop learner on natural-query bank rows, with full native baseline fidelity and frozen reader/Copy/cue/prefix parameters. A zero-update full128 admission and actual B8 cost probe precede fitting; a narrow Rust preparation example independently reloads and seals the chosen reader binding.\n\nAt numerical source fa8b8137, one64-update/B8 fit increases complete development replies11→23/128 (12 gains/no losses); exposed diagnostic remains1/32. Across1268 matched canonical positions, rawCopy, cue/prefix, source selection and angular indices are unchanged. This is a boundary-calibration component result, not improved retrieval, transfer or chat. Preserve the calibrated endpoint; next investigate geometric query/source binding because58 remaining payload failures occur at the first token.\n\nValidation on uor-step6 Linux x86 CPU16/noGPU at fa8b8137: actual signed warm-start library test1/PASS, observation configuration test1/PASS, all26 bank-fit driver tests/PASS, release builds, independent selected-reader reload and native baseline parity. Fit exit0 in243.849s, firstpacked crossing46, selected64 by baseline-inclusive development CE. A zero-match test filter and transport/cache/authorization setup failures are explicitly corrected/retained. The later bc052043 commit changes documentation only; final PR-head checks and parent1745 protected delivery remain pending, so this stays draft.\n\nComplete evidence and limitations: docs/integration/geometric-endpoint-calibration-2026-10-05.md. Returned archive SHA c631c75b…, cloud-store endpoint-calibration-20261005-1 MD5 123fa804498b1be020fe25a6b170bdfc. Shared compiler/session seams untouched. References #820 and #1552.\n",
